{"title":"2024 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_1_Scholars_Foundation_(Easy_to_Understand)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by 1 Scholars Foundation (Easy to Understand)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the product of all the positive integer divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. What is the units digit\nof <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e20e979179cdbb8e9ab6f597ab0b24cbe0a187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 4\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 6\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55fded34b435e6143b0f3c61922ab53d0a75ffae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 14, 21, 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" />. Multiply the unit digits to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c024459b191f13b58f34b5e366d4e49e32cad7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product of the factors of a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/137b19900d4da1af0b77a88e1a04ca23f87c3535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^\\frac{\\tau(n)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456f051f0d6a8b0f2745b1cd63a4b26003858880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/485ef0b9362d384602e372802c563451b4cd6c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42 = 2^1 \\cdot 3^1 \\cdot 7^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/322233e7fa8afad9d2e7fdd6c986ee9cacca5fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+1)(1+1)(1+1) = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" /> factors, so the product of the divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7c093ae411c356bc62c21fb065b0d045c260d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[42^{\\frac{8}{2}} \\equiv 42^4 \\equiv 2^4 \\equiv 16 \\equiv \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 6} \\pmod{10}.\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The factors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55fded34b435e6143b0f3c61922ab53d0a75ffae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 14, 21, 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" />. We can take out the 1 giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d6f7659212a249e23511030f24102ad747cab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 6, 7, 14, 21, 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />. We can then take the unit digit of each number because the unit digit of the product is dependent on the product of the unit digits in the factors. So the new list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/a/a0adb2715f87fbdd180b8465350e66c3e56cdd80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 6, 7, 4, 1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />. Taking out the 1 again we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/1542b4ea2ec0fbed71eac8579036f771055f6678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 6, 7, 4, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />. Multiplying the first 3 numbers gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> which we take the unit digit off. Taking the final 3 digits we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> which we take the unit digit off again. This leaves us with 2 numbers which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the product of them is 36 and the unit digit of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c024459b191f13b58f34b5e366d4e49e32cad7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_1_Scholars_Foundation_.28Easy_to_Understand.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_1_Scholars_Foundation_(Easy_to_Understand)\">Video Solution by 1 Scholars Foundation (Easy to Understand)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by 1 Scholars Foundation (Easy to Understand)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/T_QESWAKUUk?si=E8c2gKO-ZVPZ2tek&amp;t=201\">https://youtu.be/T_QESWAKUUk?si=E8c2gKO-ZVPZ2tek&amp;t=201</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_Pi_Academy_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution 2 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QLziG_2e7CY\">https://youtu.be/QLziG_2e7CY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24EZaeAThuE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24EZaeAThuE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZaHv4UkXcbs?t=603\">https://youtu.be/ZaHv4UkXcbs?t=603</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" tit